<% content_for :title, "Sign in" %>

<section class="grid flex-1 items-center gap-16 py-6 md:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] md:gap-24">
  <div class="max-w-xl">
    <h1 class="font-display text-5xl font-extrabold leading-[1.02] sm:text-6xl">Does this PR need a human?</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-md text-lg leading-relaxed text-base-content/75">
      Pick a pull request from your GitHub repositories. Jev reads the changes and tags it for a human review, an LLM review, or no review at all.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10">
      <% if github_sign_in_configured? && !DevelopmentPreview.enabled? %>
        <%= button_to "/auth/github", class: "btn btn-primary btn-lg", data: { turbo: false } do %>
          <%= lucide_icon "github", class: "size-5", "aria-hidden": true %>
          Continue with GitHub
        <% end %>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-base-content/60">We read your repositories and pull requests. Nothing is written to GitHub.</p>
      <% elsif DevelopmentPreview.enabled? %>
        <%= button_to preview_session_path, class: "btn btn-primary btn-lg" do %>
          <%= lucide_icon "flask-conical", class: "size-5", "aria-hidden": true %>
          Try with sample data
        <% end %>
        <div role="alert" class="alert alert-warning alert-soft mt-4 max-w-md">
          <%= lucide_icon "key-round", class: "size-5", "aria-hidden": true %>
          <span>GitHub or Jev credentials are missing, so this is sample data. Nothing is sent to either. Add the GitHub OAuth app and <code>typesafe.api_key</code> (or <code>GITHUB_CLIENT_ID</code>, <code>GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET</code>, and <code>TYPESAFE_API_KEY</code>) and restart to use the real ones.</span>
        </div>
      <% else %>
        <div role="alert" class="alert alert-warning alert-soft max-w-md">
          <%= lucide_icon "key-round", class: "size-5", "aria-hidden": true %>
          <span>GitHub sign-in isn't set up. Add <code>github.client_id</code> and <code>github.client_secret</code> with <code>bin/rails credentials:edit</code> (or set <code>GITHUB_CLIENT_ID</code> and <code>GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET</code>), then restart the server.</span>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-md text-sm leading-relaxed text-base-content/60">
      Verdicts are shared with people who currently have GitHub access to the repository. Votes and reasons stay private.
      Deleting your account removes personal data; shared verdicts and PR/file metadata stay without a link to your account.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="triage-tag-stage md:pt-4">
    <%= render "shared/triage_tag", settle: true %>
  </div>
</section>
